{"attack": true, "case": "The target's claim that the dilemma 'dissolves' is directly contradicted by its own enumerated counterconditions. The mechanism asserts action follows because 'all alternatives have been eliminated,' but the first countercondition explicitly admits that multiple unrefuted theories may remain, in which case elimination does not yield a unique default. The eliminative-default story only dissolves the dilemma in the special case where exactly one theory survives; in the general case the agent still faces a choice the mechanism cannot arbitrate. Thus the claim overstates its scope: it does not dissolve the dilemma, it merely narrows it. Additionally, the mechanism's conclusion that 'the underlying structure was never relevant to the outcome at all' is a non sequitur — even granting that action defaults to unrefuted theories, the process by which theories were refuted (test severity, scope of criticism) determines which theories survive and therefore directly shapes the outcome.", "counterexample": ["Two theories, A and B, both survive all past criticism; no further evidence eliminates either. The eliminative default provides no basis for action, so the dilemma is not dissolved but merely relocated to the choice between surviving theories."], "premise": "The target claims the dilemma dissolves under the eliminative-default view, yet its own counterconditions identify live cases (multiple unrefuted theories; variable cost requiring probability estimates) where elimination alone fails to determine action.", "premise_evidence": [{"block": "11fd270f78fc9c8ef266254883a098c65a0b1f775b68cf58aca773f911416629", "quote": "The dilemma dissolves if we view corroboration reports not as guides to action, but as historical records of criticism; the 'preference' is simply the refusal to act on already-refuted theories, leaving only the unrefuted ones by default."}, {"block": "11fd270f78fc9c8ef266254883a098c65a0b1f775b68cf58aca773f911416629", "quote": "Eliminative Default: Action is not taken *because* a theory is corroborated, but because all alternatives have been eliminated. Corroboration is merely the label for 'not yet eliminated'. It follows that the underlying structure was never relevant to the outcome at all."}], "successor_question": "When elimination leaves multiple unrefuted theories, what principled mechanism — if any — does the eliminative-default view provide for selecting among them without reintroducing exactly the probabilistic or structural reasoning it claims to dispense with?"}